---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHero from '../../components/PageHero.astro';
import CTA from '../../components/CTA.astro';
import Trust from '../../components/Trust.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Network"
  description="The Lattix lattice: one connection for laboratories, imaging groups, and EHRs. Coverage compounds as partners join — including national networks on the same interface."
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="Network"
    title="Connect once. Coverage compounds."
    lede="Every laboratory, imaging group, and EHR that joins the lattice is available to everyone already on it. The next partner is not another six-month project."
    image="/images/network-city.jpg"
    secondaryHref="/security"
    secondaryLabel="Security & compliance"
  />

  <section class="bg-paper px-5 py-24 sm:px-8">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl">
      <h2 class="max-w-3xl font-serif text-4xl tracking-tight sm:text-5xl">
        Density first. Nationals on the same pipes.
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-6 max-w-2xl text-lg text-ink/70">
        The lattice is designed so regional and specialty partners — the ones outpatient care can
        actually reach — come on first. National reference laboratories, imaging networks, and
        e-prescribing rails use the same technical integration when volume and diligence line up.
        You should not start over when they do.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-12 grid gap-5 md:grid-cols-2">
        <article class="rounded-2xl border border-ink/8 bg-cream p-8">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-medium">Regional and specialty partners</h3>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink/65">
            Independent laboratories, specialty diagnostics, and imaging groups that lose orders
            because EHRs will not build a one-off interface. They join once and take work from
            every care organization on the lattice.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="rounded-2xl border border-ink/8 bg-cream p-8">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-medium">National networks, same interface</h3>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink/65">
            The largest diagnostic and e-prescribing networks are gated on volume, security, and
            time. The lattice is built so those connections are an expansion of the same pipes —
            not a second product your customers have to wait for.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="rounded-2xl border border-ink/8 bg-cream p-8">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-medium">EHRs as demand nodes</h3>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink/65">
            Outpatient and digital health platforms bring order volume. Diagnostic partners bring
            supply. Each side makes the other more valuable without a bilateral project for every
            pair.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="rounded-2xl border border-ink/8 bg-cream p-8">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-medium">Built for the frameworks that come next</h3>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink/65">
            FHIR, HL7 v2, purposes of use, audit, and BAAs are the floor. The same lattice is
            designed to sit under TEFCA and state data-sharing frameworks when those become the
            path a partner needs.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-cream px-5 py-24 sm:px-8">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-4xl tracking-tight">Purposes of use</h2>
      <div class="mt-10 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-3">
        {
          [
            { t: 'Treatment', d: 'Orders, results, and records for patients you are treating.' },
            { t: 'Operations', d: 'Authorized exchange to run the diagnostic loop — compendiums, routing, delivery.' },
            { t: 'Payment', d: 'Billing context on the order, returned with the result, under a BAA.' },
          ].map((p) => (
            <article class="rounded-2xl border border-ink/8 bg-paper p-6">
              <h3 class="font-medium">{p.t}</h3>
              <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-ink/65">{p.d}</p>
            </article>
          ))
        }
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Trust />
  <CTA />
</Base>
